    <!-- FAQ Structured Data (JSON-LD) -->
    <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a destination wedding in Udaipur cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A destination wedding in Udaipur typically ranges from ₹50 lakh to ₹5 crore depending on the venue, guest count, and number of events. A boutique palace wedding for 80–100 guests over 2 days starts around ₹80 lakh–₹1.2 crore. A full palace buyout at a property like Taj Lake Palace or Oberoi Udaivilas for 150–180 guests in peak season can reach ₹4–5 crore. The single biggest variable is the hotel room buyout — which forms 40–50% of the total cost at most premium properties."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How far in advance should we book a wedding planner in India?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For a peak season wedding (November to February), we recommend starting the planning process 15–18 months in advance. The most sought-after venues — particularly palace properties in Udaipur and Jaipur — are often fully booked 12–14 months ahead. Off-season weddings (March–June) can sometimes be planned in 8–10 months. At Regal Weddings, we take on only 8 handpicked projects per year, so availability is limited regardless of timing."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which is better for a destination wedding — Udaipur, Jaipur or Goa?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Each destination has a distinct personality. Udaipur — the City of Lakes — offers palace hotels on the water's edge, best suited for 80–200 guests. Jaipur — the Pink City — provides grand forts and larger palace properties, ideal for bigger guest counts. Goa suits couples wanting a beach and sun-soaked celebration with a relaxed, resort vibe. Regal Weddings has planned weddings across all three for over 23 years."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you plan weddings for NRI and overseas couples?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes — the majority of our clients are NRI and international couples based in the UK, USA, Canada, Australia, and the Middle East. We completely adapt our working hours to your time zone and handle every ground-level detail in India so you never have to. From venue shortlisting and vendor coordination to guest logistics and on-site execution — we manage it all."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How many guests can a destination wedding in India accommodate?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most premium palace and resort properties we work with are suited for 50 to 300 guests. Intimate boutique weddings of 40–80 guests unlock smaller, exclusive heritage properties and allow for a more curated experience. Larger celebrations of 200–300+ guests are well-suited to properties like Samode Palace or Jai Mahal Palace in Jaipur."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What does Regal Weddings' planning fee include?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Our planning fee covers the full scope of wedding management: initial consultation and destination selection, venue shortlisting and contract negotiation, vendor sourcing and management (décor, photography, catering, entertainment, MUA), guest logistics and accommodation coordination, event-by-event run sheets, on-site presence across all wedding days, and post-wedding wrap-up."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
    </script>

